Third-party content inside those files, and its terms
-----------------------------------------------------
- RIPL (IAEA, RIPL-3 / RIPL-4): incognita_emu/meta/sfunc_ripl.csv holds measured neutron strength functions S0/S1 as
  compiled in RIPL-3 and in the RIPL-4 resonance files (Mughabghab-2018 column). IAEA-NDS terms: scientific reuse with
  attribution. Cite: R. Capote et al., Nucl. Data Sheets 110 (2009) 3107, and the RIPL-4 repository
  (https://github.com/IAEA-NDS/RIPL-4).
- TALYS (MIT licence, A. Koning et al.): the engine is a port. The TALYS structure database is not redistributed; users
  download it (scripts/make_structure.sh).

No evaluated nuclear-data library values (ENDF/B, JENDL, JEFF, TENDL, ...) are distributed in this repository.
